# Build output. Every Dockerfile that builds from the repository root
# (examples/deploy-agent, itk/Dockerfile.rust-agent, itk/Dockerfile.tck)
# copies the source and compiles inside the image, so a host `target/` is
# never needed there — it only made the build context gigabytes larger and,
# for the musl images, carried glibc artifacts in. `**/` also covers the
# per-agent directories under benches/sdk-comparison/harness.
**/target

# Secrets and local configuration a developer keeps beside the source: none
# belongs in a build context, where every stage that copies the tree keeps
# it in a layer and in the build cache (audit A12, 2026-10-29).
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx

# History, editor state and things no build reads: excluded so a commit or
# a book edit does not invalidate the `COPY . .` layers and rebuild the
# workspace.
.git
.github
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode
book/book
book/static
